-- title:
--   Constructing the exact children of a valid reporting prefix
-- statement:
--   Let a global output have $J$ rows $Q_j$, each a $2h$-subset of a $512h$-element block. A valid prefix $u$ of length $k<J$ chooses an $h$-subset of each of the first $k$ rows. Put $L=J(512h)$ and $G=\binom{2h}h$. Reserve consecutive, possibly gapped, arrays of length $G$ at bases $m,a,b$, ending before scratch $w$: $m+G\le a$, $a+G\le b$, $b+G\le w$.
--
--   Assume $w+2L+2\le S\le W$, $2^{L+1}\le W$, and $d+L+3\le D$. The fixed constructor enumerates the $h$-subsets $T_i$ of row $k$ and writes
--   $$\nu(m+i)=\operatorname{mask}(T_i),\quad\nu(a+i)=\operatorname{mask}(L_u\cup T_i),\quad\nu(b+i)=\operatorname{mask}(R_u\cup(Q_k\setminus T_i)).$$
--   Masks use global block coordinates. It returns the remaining-query mask after row $k$, preserves cells below $m$, and meets the defined child-construction budget.
--
--   The array order is exactly the abstract list of valid extended prefixes.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/c0ldzy17/three-sum-lean/blob/2b639655e07421b9ac743de9090459bab473a7c0/Submission/ThreeSum/LightBlockChildrenIndexed.lean#L97-L138

